)

mti_ecm_dp_profile_action(...)
}
\arguments{
\item{y}{Numeric univariate response sample.}

\item{content}{Required population content.}

\item{posterior_confidence}{Required posterior probability that the selected
interval has at least \code{content} population mass under the direct-DP
response-distribution posterior.}

\item{dp_concentration}{Positive direct-DP concentration.}

\item{dp_base_measure}{Base measure from \code{\link{rqr_dp_base_normal}} or a
compatible object.}

\item{strict_bayes}{Reject data-dependent DP base measures.}

\item{scan_target_content}{Optional scan-calibrated fitted content used only
as an upper reference for the MTI profile grid.}

\item{q_grid}{Optional fitted-content grid. If \code{NULL}, a deterministic
grid is built from \code{content}, sample size, and
\code{scan_target_content}.}

\item{q_grid_control}{List with \code{n_points}, \code{q_min_buffer},
\code{q_max}, and \code{include_scan_target}.}

\item{tilt_grid_control}{List with \code{tilt_offsets_sd},
\code{include_zero_tilt}, and \code{max_abs_tilt_sd}.}

\item{learning_rate}{Fixed generalized-Bayes learning rate for MTI-ECM.}

\item{beta_prior_obj}{Ridge beta prior object. Defaults to a weak ridge prior.}

\item{ecm_control}{ECM control list. For iid validation, use
\code{ecm_backend = "cpp"}.}

\item{expand_if_empty}{Expand the profile grid once if no candidate passes the
DP screen.}

\item{return_candidate_traces}{Return per-iteration ECM traces for every
fitted profile candidate. This option is intended for focused diagnostics and
is \code{FALSE} by default to keep validation outputs compact.}

\item{na_rm}{Remove missing responses.}

\item{...}{Arguments passed to \code{rqr_mti_ecm_dp_profile_action()}.}
}
\value{
An \code{rqr_mti_ecm_dp_profile_action} object with the selected interval,
candidate table, optional candidate traces, direct-DP content probabilities,
ECM diagnostics, and provenance fields.
}
\description{
Searches fixed-target MTI-ECM endpoint candidates over a grid of fitted
contents and mean tilts, then screens the resulting intervals with the exact
direct-DP posterior content probability for fixed intervals.
}
\details{
The MTI-ECM layer is a loss-based generalized-Bayes endpoint construction. The
direct-DP layer is an ordinary response-distribution model used to evaluate
interval content. The selected interval is therefore Bayesian content
calibrated and empirically validated by repeated-sampling studies; it is not
an exact distribution-free scan tolerance action.
}
